\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  In my baptism, I'm glad
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 even more so than my own birth.
\par And the Lord by His own life
\par gave me all the spirit in it
\par That I might not only be
\par Man, but turn to be God's own.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  Hitherto the Almighty
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 breathed into my nose for my life
\par again He used His spirit
\par in my baptism for new life
\par I had life on that birth day
\par now is ever lasting life.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  I was initiated on
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 my baptism, true in God's name
\par And I became god's own son
\par that Jesus has bought with His blood
\par So the spirit in the Lord
\par has been imparted to me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par    4.  Whenever trouble appears
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0    I'll rejoice in my baptism
\par    When my death is drawing near,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0   that will be my soul comforter.
\par   I have an identity
\par \pard       as a royal of the Lord.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

